Editorial work on Volume 8,
on family and kinship, for the nine-volume series, <em>Freedom: A Documentary
History of Emancipation, 1861-1867</em>. See website at <a href="http://www.freedmen.umd.edu/">http://www.freedmen.umd.edu/</a>.&nbsp;

A
study of the Nobel-prize-winning British writer Rudyard Kipling&rsquo;s engagement with the United States, especially during four
years he spent living in Vermont. By focusing on Kipling's "American decade" (1889-99), the book will provide a fresh perspective on Kipling's life and works, as well as on the American Gilded Age.&nbsp;

A planning process at Wayne State University that builds faculty buy-in for
rethinking graduate education by creating a cohort of &ldquo;Next Generation Faculty
Fellows.&rdquo;&nbsp;

Planning at the
University of Rhode Island (URI) around four topics: 1) potential approaches to stimulate collaboration between programs,
departments, and schools; 2) methods for initiating partnerships with non-academic
institutions; 3) exploration of altered formats or requirements for the PhD dissertation;
and 4) identification of humanities PhD alumni in various fields to advise or
mentor graduate students.&nbsp;&nbsp;

